    "mistake.001.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spend three seconds thinking about what the variable actually holds. Put its role in the name: userProfileList instead of data, formattedDate instead of temp, filteredActiveUsers instead of result. The goal is code that reads like an English sentence. For example, if (isUserActive && hasPermission) tells you what it means just by reading the condition."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spend three seconds asking \"what does this variable actually hold?\" whenever you name one. Put its role in the name: userProfileList instead of data, formattedDate instead of temp, filteredActiveUsers instead of result. The aim is code that reads like an English sentence. For instance, if (isUserActive && hasPermission) tells you what it means just by reading it."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "변수명을 지을 때 '이 변수가 무엇을 담고 있는지' 3초만 생각해보세요. data 대신 userProfileList, temp 대신 formattedDate, result 대신 filteredActiveUsers처럼 역할을 이름에 담으세요. 코드를 영어 문장처럼 읽히게 만드는 것이 목표입니다. 예를 들어 if (isUserActive && hasPermission)은 조건문을 읽는 것만으로 의미가 파악됩니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "起变量名时，花 3 秒想一想“这个变量里装的是什么”。用 userProfileList 代替 data，用 formattedDate 代替 temp，用 filteredActiveUsers 代替 result，把变量的作用写进名字里。目标是让代码读起来像一句英文。比如 if (isUserActive && hasPermission)，光读条件语句就能明白意思。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.001.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Code is read ten times more often than it is written. A good name is more powerful than a comment. Agree on naming conventions (camelCase, snake_case, and so on) with your team, avoid abbreviations (usr → user, btn → button), and use names you can search for. This one habit alone dramatically improves code review speed and maintainability."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You spend ten times longer reading code than writing it. A good name is more powerful than a comment. Agree naming conventions (camelCase, snake_case and so on) with your team, avoid abbreviations (usr becomes user, btn becomes button) and choose names that are easy to search for. This one habit alone dramatically improves code review speed and maintainability."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "코드는 쓰는 시간보다 읽는 시간이 10배 많습니다. 좋은 이름은 주석보다 강력합니다. 명명 규칙(camelCase, snake_case 등)을 팀과 통일하고, 약어를 피하며(usr → user, btn → button), 검색 가능한 이름을 사용하세요. 이 습관 하나만으로도 코드 리뷰 속도와 유지보수성이 극적으로 향상됩니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "代码被阅读的时间是编写时间的 10 倍。好名字比注释更有力。和团队统一命名规范（camelCase、snake_case 等），避免缩写（usr → user、btn → button），使用方便搜索的名字。光是这一个习惯，就能大幅提升代码评审的速度和可维护性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
