    "mistake.001.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you write code in a hurry, you fall into the habit of naming things temp, data, result, and val. At the moment you write them, the context is in your head, so it feels fine. But a week later you're re-reading the code from the top, wondering, 'What was this variable again?'"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you write code quickly, you fall into the habit of using names such as temp, data, result and val. In the moment it's fine, because the context is in your head, but a week later you find yourself wondering \"what was this variable?\" and rereading the code from the top."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "빠르게 코드를 작성하다 보면 temp, data, result, val 같은 이름을 습관적으로 사용하게 됩니다. 작성하는 순간에는 맥락이 머릿속에 있어 문제가 없지만, 일주일만 지나도 '이 변수가 뭐였지?' 하고 코드를 처음부터 다시 읽어야 합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "赶着写代码时，会下意识地用 temp、data、result、val 这类名字。写的时候上下文都在脑子里，没什么问题；可是过了一周，你就得把代码从头读一遍才想得起“这个变量是干嘛的？”。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.002.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Consider splitting a function once it passes 20 lines. The test is: can you describe what this function does in one sentence? Split each step into its own function, like validateUserInput(), transformToAPIFormat(), callPaymentAPI(), and formatResponse(), and let the main function act only as an orchestrator that calls them in order."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Consider splitting a function once it goes beyond 20 lines. The test is: \"can I describe what this function does in one sentence?\" Separate each step into its own function, such as validateUserInput(), transformToAPIFormat(), callPaymentAPI() and formatResponse(), and let the main function simply act as an orchestrator that calls them in order."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "함수 하나가 20줄을 넘으면 분리 시점을 검토하세요. '이 함수가 하는 일을 한 문장으로 설명할 수 있는가?'가 기준입니다. validateUserInput(), transformToAPIFormat(), callPaymentAPI(), formatResponse()처럼 각 단계를 독립적인 함수로 분리하고, 메인 함수는 이들을 순서대로 호출하는 오케스트레이터 역할만 하게 만드세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "函数一超过 20 行，就该考虑拆分了。判断标准是：这个函数做的事，能不能用一句话说清楚？把每个步骤拆成独立的函数，比如 validateUserInput()、transformToAPIFormat()、callPaymentAPI()、formatResponse()，主函数只负责按顺序调用它们，像个调度者。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.002.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You learn the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) by doing. A small function reveals its role through its name, can be tested on its own, and can be reused elsewhere. Structuring code so it reads like a story is a core skill of senior developers."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You get a real feel for the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP). A small function reveals its purpose through its name alone, can be tested independently and can be reused elsewhere. Being able to structure code so that it reads like a story is a core skill of senior developers."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "단일 책임 원칙(SRP)을 몸으로 익히게 됩니다. 작은 함수는 이름만으로 역할이 드러나고, 독립적으로 테스트할 수 있으며, 다른 곳에서 재사용할 수 있습니다. 코드를 '이야기'처럼 읽을 수 있게 구조화하는 능력은 시니어 개발자의 핵심 역량입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会真正掌握单一职责原则（SRP）。小函数光看名字就知道做什么，可以独立测试，也能在别处复用。把代码组织得像讲故事一样好读，是资深开发者的核心能力。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
