    "mistake.002.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "While implementing one feature, you write input validation, data transformation, the API call, result processing, and error handling all in one function. At first the flow is easy to see, but once the function passes 200 lines, it's hard to find what to change, and side effects become impossible to predict."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "While building one feature, you put input validation, data transformation, the API call, result processing and error handling all into one function. At first you can see the whole flow, but once it passes 200 lines it's hard to know where to make a change, and the side effects become impossible to predict."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "기능 하나를 구현하면서 입력 검증, 데이터 변환, API 호출, 결과 가공, 에러 처리를 모두 한 함수에 작성합니다. 처음에는 흐름이 눈에 보이지만, 함수가 200줄을 넘어가면 수정할 때 어디를 고쳐야 할지 찾기 어렵고, 사이드 이펙트를 예측할 수 없게 됩니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "实现一个功能时，把输入校验、数据转换、API 调用、结果处理、错误处理全写进同一个函数。刚开始流程还一目了然，可函数一旦超过 200 行，改的时候就很难找到该改哪里，副作用也无法预料。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.003.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The moment you want to copy and paste is the signal to refactor. Extract the shared logic into a function or class, and pass only what differs as parameters or callbacks. Once something repeats three times (the Rule of Three), you should definitely abstract it. For example, a single fetchList(endpoint, transformer) can handle many kinds of list queries."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The moment you want to copy and paste is your cue to refactor. Extract the common logic into a function or class and pass only the parts that differ as parameters or callbacks. Once something repeats three times (the Rule of Three), you really must abstract it. For example, a single fetchList(endpoint, transformer) can handle several list lookups."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "코드를 복붙하려는 순간이 리팩토링의 신호입니다. 공통 로직을 함수나 클래스로 추출하고, 달라지는 부분만 매개변수나 콜백으로 전달하세요. 반복이 3번 이상이면(Rule of Three) 반드시 추상화해야 합니다. 예를 들어 fetchList(endpoint, transformer) 하나로 여러 목록 조회를 처리할 수 있습니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一想复制粘贴，就是该重构的信号。把公共逻辑提取成函数或类，只把不同的部分通过参数或回调传进去。重复出现 3 次以上（Rule of Three）就一定要抽象。比如一个 fetchList(endpoint, transformer) 就能处理多种列表查询。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.003.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You build the DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle and the ability to abstract. Over-abstraction is dangerous too, so ask: is this code really changing together for the same reason? The right abstraction doesn't shrink the amount of code; it lowers the cost of change."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You build up the DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle and the ability to abstract. Over-abstraction is dangerous too, so judge by asking \"is this code genuinely going to change together, for the same reason?\" The right abstraction doesn't reduce the amount of code; it reduces the cost of change."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "DRY(Don't Repeat Yourself) 원칙과 추상화 능력을 기르게 됩니다. 다만 과도한 추상화도 위험하므로, '정말 같은 이유로 같이 변경되는 코드인가?'를 기준으로 판단하세요. 올바른 추상화는 코드량을 줄이는 것이 아니라, 변경 비용을 줄이는 것입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会培养 DRY（Don't Repeat Yourself）原则和抽象能力。不过过度抽象同样危险，要以“这些代码真的会因为同一个原因一起变化吗？”作为判断标准。正确的抽象，不是为了减少代码量，而是为了降低修改成本。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
