    "mistake.012.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When a red error appears, you reflexively copy the entire message and paste it into Google. You find a Stack Overflow answer and apply it, but the error message itself said exactly what and where the problem was: 'line 42: variable userName is not defined'."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When a red error appears, you reflexively copy the whole message and paste it into Google. You find a Stack Overflow answer and apply it, when the error message itself said exactly what the cause and location were: \"line 42: variable userName is not defined\"."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "빨간 에러가 터지면 반사적으로 에러 메시지 전체를 복사해서 구글에 붙여넣습니다. 스택오버플로우 답변을 찾아 적용하지만, 정작 에러 메시지에 'line 42: variable userName is not defined'라고 정확히 원인과 위치가 적혀 있었습니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一出现红色报错，就条件反射地把整段错误信息复制去搜索。找到 Stack Overflow 的回答就照着用，可其实错误信息里明明写着“line 42: variable userName is not defined”，原因和位置都写得清清楚楚。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.013.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apply a scientific debugging method. 1) Observe the symptom precisely. 2) Form a hypothesis ('This variable is null, so it errors'). 3) Test the hypothesis (check with a debugger or build a minimal reproduction). 4) If it's right, fix it; if it's wrong, form a new hypothesis. A bisect strategy helps too: check the state at the midpoint of the code and narrow the range."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apply a scientific method to debugging. 1) Observe the symptoms precisely. 2) Form a hypothesis (\"this variable is null, so it throws an error\"). 3) Test the hypothesis (check with the debugger, or build a minimal reproduction). 4) If it holds, fix it; if not, form a new one. A bisect strategy helps too: check the state at the midpoint of the code and narrow the range step by step."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "과학적 디버깅 방법론을 적용하세요. 1) 현상을 정확히 관찰한다, 2) 가설을 세운다('이 변수가 null이어서 에러가 날 것이다'), 3) 가설을 검증한다(디버거로 확인하거나, 최소 재현 코드를 만든다), 4) 가설이 맞으면 수정, 틀리면 새 가설을 세운다. 이진 탐색(bisect) 전략도 유용합니다. 코드의 중간 지점에서 상태를 확인하며 범위를 좁혀가세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "用科学的调试方法。1) 准确观察现象；2) 提出假设（“这个变量是 null，所以才报错”）；3) 验证假设（用调试器确认，或写出最小复现代码）；4) 假设成立就修复，不成立就提出新假设。二分（bisect）策略也很有用：在代码中间检查状态，逐步缩小范围。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.013.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You build logical thinking and systematic problem-solving. This method applies to every complex problem, not just development. This systematic approach to debugging is one of the core skills that set senior developers apart."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You build logical thinking and systematic problem-solving. This method applies not only to development but to solving any complex problem. This systematic approach to debugging is one of the key abilities that set senior developers apart."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "논리적 사고력과 체계적 문제 해결 능력을 기릅니다. 이 방법론은 개발뿐 아니라 모든 복잡한 문제 해결에 적용됩니다. 시니어 개발자를 구분 짓는 핵심 역량 중 하나가 바로 이 체계적 디버깅 능력입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会培养逻辑思维和系统解决问题的能力。这套方法不仅适用于开发，也适用于一切复杂问题的解决。系统化的调试能力，正是区分资深开发者的核心能力之一。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
