    "mistake.023.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You skip making a branch and work and push directly on main. Code that goes in without a code review breaks the build, conflicts with a teammate's work, or ships unfinished code to production."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You work and push straight to main without creating a separate branch. Code that went in without a code review breaks the build, clashes with a teammate's work, or sends unfinished code out to production."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "브랜치를 따로 만들지 않고 main에서 직접 작업하고 푸시합니다. 코드 리뷰 없이 반영된 코드가 빌드를 깨뜨리거나, 다른 팀원의 작업과 충돌하거나, 미완성 코드가 프로덕션으로 나갑니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "不新建分支，直接在 main 上工作并推送。没经过评审就合入的代码破坏了构建，和同事的工作冲突，或者未完成的代码直接上了生产。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.024.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Resolve conflicts only after you understand the intent of both changes. If a conflict is complicated, ask the author of that code directly. After resolving, always run the tests to confirm the two changes were integrated correctly."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Resolve conflicts only once you understand the intent of both changes. If a conflict is complicated, ask the author of that code directly. After resolving it, always run the tests to confirm that the two changes have been integrated correctly."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "충돌 해결 시 양쪽 변경의 의도를 모두 이해한 상태에서 진행하세요. 충돌이 복잡하면 해당 코드 작성자에게 직접 물어보세요. 충돌 해결 후에는 반드시 테스트를 실행해서 두 변경이 올바르게 통합되었는지 확인하세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "解决冲突时，要先理解双方改动的意图。冲突复杂，就直接去问代码的作者。解决后一定要跑测试，确认两处改动已正确整合。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.024.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You learn to understand the context of code and the importance of communication. A conflict is a sign that two people cared about the same part, so you can use it as a chance to find ways to improve the design."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You learn how to understand the context of code and how much communication matters. A conflict is a sign that two people cared about the same part, so you can use it as a chance to find ways to improve the design."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "코드의 맥락을 이해하는 능력과 커뮤니케이션의 중요성을 배웁니다. 충돌은 두 사람이 같은 부분에 관심을 가졌다는 신호이므로, 이를 통해 설계 개선점을 발견하는 기회로 활용할 수 있습니다."
          }
