    "mistake.029.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A PR with 200 lines of changes has just the title 'Fix bug' and no description. The reviewer can't tell why the change is needed, which approach you chose and why, or how you tested it, so a meaningful review is impossible."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A PR with 200 changed lines has only the title \"Fix bug\" and no description. The reviewer can't tell why the change is needed, what approach was chosen and why, or how it was tested, so a meaningful review is impossible."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "200줄 변경이 있는 PR에 제목만 'Fix bug'이고 설명이 없습니다. 리뷰어는 왜 이 변경이 필요한지, 어떤 방법을 선택했고 왜인지, 어떻게 테스트했는지 알 수 없어 의미 있는 리뷰가 불가능합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一个改了 200 行的 PR，标题只有“Fix bug”，没有任何说明。评审者不知道为什么需要这个改动、选了什么方案、为什么这样选、怎么测的，根本没法做有意义的评审。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.030.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Understand the difference between the two strategies clearly. Merge preserves history as it happened, while rebase straightens history into a line. Never rebase shared branches (main, develop). Use rebase only on your personal feature branches, and agree on one strategy (rebase vs. merge) across the team."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Understand clearly the difference between the two strategies. Merge preserves the history as it happened, while rebase tidies the history into a straight line. Never rebase a shared branch (main, develop). Use rebase only on your own feature branches, and agree one strategy (rebase or merge) across the team."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "두 전략의 차이를 명확히 이해하세요. Merge는 히스토리를 있는 그대로 보존하고, Rebase는 히스토리를 선형으로 정리합니다. 공유 브랜치(main, develop)는 절대 rebase하지 마세요. 개인 feature 브랜치에서만 rebase를 사용하고, 팀의 전략(rebase vs merge)을 통일하세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "要清楚两种策略的区别。Merge 原样保留历史，Rebase 把历史整理成一条直线。共享分支（main、develop）绝对不要 rebase。只在个人 feature 分支上使用 rebase，并统一团队的策略（rebase 还是 merge）。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.030.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You come to understand how Git works internally (the commit graph, HEAD, refs). With that understanding, you can stay calm and sort out any complicated Git situation."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You come to understand how Git works internally (the commit graph, HEAD, references). With that understanding, you can stay calm and sort out even complicated Git situations."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Git의 내부 동작 원리(커밋 그래프, HEAD, 참조)를 이해하게 됩니다. 이 이해가 있으면 어떤 복잡한 Git 상황에서도 당황하지 않고 해결할 수 있습니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
