          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.032.retro.1" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Is there code in your project written 'for the future' that is never actually used? How much?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Is there code in your current project written \"for the future\" that isn't actually used? How much?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "현재 프로젝트에서 실제로 사용되지 않는 '미래를 위한' 코드가 있나요? 얼마나 되나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "当前项目里，有没有实际没用上、“为未来准备”的代码？有多少？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.032.retro.2" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has over-engineering ever slowed down your development? Which part was it?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has over-engineering ever slowed you down? Which part was it?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "오버엔지니어링으로 인해 개발 속도가 느려진 경험이 있나요? 어떤 부분이었나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有没有因为过度设计而拖慢开发速度的经历？是哪部分？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.032.retro.3" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Is the complexity of your current system appropriate for the business needs?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Is the complexity of your current system appropriate for the needs of the business?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "현재 시스템의 복잡도가 비즈니스 요구에 비해 적절한 수준인가요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "当前系统的复杂度，相对于业务需求来说合适吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.032.retro.4" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How do you decide where the line is between what you need now and what you might need later?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How do you judge where \"what we need now\" ends and \"what we might need later\" begins?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "'지금 필요한 것'과 '나중에 필요할 수 있는 것'의 경계를 어떻게 판단하고 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你怎么判断“现在需要的”和“以后可能需要的”之间的界限？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.032.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "For a service with 100 users, you apply microservices, event-driven architecture, and CQRS. Managing infrastructure and service-to-service communication problems eat more time than the actual business development. Two team members manage 10 services."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You apply microservices, event-driven architecture and CQRS to a service with 100 users. Managing the infrastructure and sorting out communication between services eats more time than the actual business development. Two team members are looking after ten services."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "사용자 100명인 서비스에 마이크로서비스, 이벤트 드리븐 아키텍처, CQRS를 적용합니다. 인프라 관리와 서비스 간 통신 문제가 실제 비즈니스 개발보다 더 많은 시간을 소모합니다. 팀원 2명이 10개 서비스를 관리합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一个只有 100 个用户的服务，却上了微服务、事件驱动架构和 CQRS。基础设施管理和服务间通信问题，比真正的业务开发还要耗时间。2 个人的团队在维护 10 个服务。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.033.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The problem comes first and the solution second. The right approach is to ask, 'Is there a pattern that fits this problem?' not 'Where can I use this pattern?' Let patterns emerge naturally during refactoring. Before applying a pattern, always ask yourself whether there's a simpler way without it."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "With patterns, the problem comes first and the solution second. The right approach is \"is there a pattern that fits this problem?\", not \"where can I use this pattern?\" Let patterns emerge naturally during refactoring. Before applying a pattern, always ask yourself: \"is there a simpler way without it?\""
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "패턴은 문제가 먼저이고 해결책이 나중입니다. '이 문제에 맞는 패턴이 있을까?'가 올바른 접근이지, '이 패턴을 어디에 쓸 수 있을까?'가 아닙니다. 리팩토링 과정에서 자연스럽게 패턴이 등장하게 하세요. 패턴 적용 전에 '이 패턴 없이 더 간단한 방법은 없는가?'를 반드시 검토하세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "先有问题，后有模式。正确的思路是“针对这个问题有没有合适的模式？”，而不是“这个模式能用在哪里？”。让模式在重构过程中自然出现。应用模式之前，一定要想一想：不用这个模式，有没有更简单的办法？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.033.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You come to understand the essence of a pattern: a proven solution to a recurring design problem. Knowing when to apply a pattern and when not to matters more than knowing its name."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You come to understand the essence of a pattern: a proven solution to a design problem that keeps recurring. Knowing the names of patterns matters less than knowing when to apply them and when not to, and that is the real skill."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "패턴의 본질(반복적으로 나타나는 설계 문제에 대한 검증된 해결책)을 이해하게 됩니다. 패턴 이름을 아는 것보다 언제 적용하고 언제 적용하지 말아야 하는지를 아는 것이 진정한 역량입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会理解模式的本质：针对反复出现的设计问题，经过验证的解决方案。比起知道模式的名字，知道什么时候该用、什么时候不该用，才是真本事。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.033.mistake" : {
