    },
    "mistake.036.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You add columns whenever you need them while developing and set up relationships loosely. Later you find the same information stored in three tables, and updating one leaves the others inconsistent. Query performance gets worse and worse."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "As you develop, you add columns whenever you need them and set up relationships carelessly. Later you discover the same information stored in three tables, and changing one leaves the others inconsistent. Query performance gets steadily worse, too."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "개발하면서 필요할 때마다 컬럼을 추가하고, 관계를 대충 설정합니다. 나중에 보니 같은 정보가 3개 테이블에 중복 저장되어 있고, 하나를 수정하면 나머지와 불일치가 발생합니다. 쿼리 성능도 점점 나빠집니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "开发时需要什么就加什么字段，关系也随便设置。后来才发现同一份信息在 3 张表里重复存储，改了一处，其余的就不一致了。查询性能也越来越差。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.037.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Don't aim for perfect scalability from day one; build a structure that can scale. Apply basic patterns like pagination, indexing, a caching layer, and asynchronous processing. And make it a habit to ask, 'What happens to this code with 100 times more data?'"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Don't aim for perfect scalability from day one; build a structure that can scale. Apply the basic patterns: pagination, indexing, a caching layer, asynchronous processing. And make a habit of asking, \"what happens to this code when there is 100 times as much data?\""
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "처음부터 완벽한 확장성이 아니라, '확장 가능한 구조'를 만드세요. 페이지네이션, 인덱싱, 캐싱 레이어, 비동기 처리 등 기본적인 패턴을 적용하세요. 그리고 '이 코드가 데이터 100배가 되면 어떻게 될까?'라는 질문을 습관적으로 던지세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一开始不必追求完美的可扩展性，而是搭建“可以扩展的结构”。应用分页、索引、缓存层、异步处理等基本模式。并养成习惯，常问自己：“数据量变成 100 倍，这段代码会怎样？”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.037.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You start thinking at scale. The difference between O(n) and O(n²) is unnoticeable with 10 records, but with a million records it decides whether your service stays available."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You start thinking at scale. The difference between O(n) and O(n²) is invisible with 10 records, but with a million it decides whether your service stays available."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "규모의 사고(Thinking at Scale)를 시작하게 됩니다. O(n)과 O(n²)의 차이가 10건에서는 느껴지지 않지만, 100만 건에서는 서비스 가용성을 결정합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会开始用规模思维（Thinking at Scale）思考问题。O(n) 和 O(n²) 的差别在 10 条数据时感觉不到，到了 100 万条，就决定了服务是否可用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.037.mistake" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Not considering scalability at all"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
