    "mistake.040.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You say, 'It works for now, so let's refactor later,' leave a TODO comment, and move on. As debt piles up, new features take longer and longer, and the system gets less stable. At some point you face the drastic choice of a full rewrite."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "\"It works for now, so we'll refactor later,\" you say, leaving only a TODO comment and moving on. As the debt builds up, adding new features takes longer and longer and the system gets less and less stable. Eventually you face the drastic option of a complete rewrite."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "'일단 돌아가니까 나중에 리팩토링하자'며 TODO 주석만 남기고 넘어갑니다. 부채가 쌓이면서 새 기능 추가에 점점 더 오래 걸리고, 시스템이 점점 불안정해집니다. 어느 순간 '전면 재작성'이라는 극단적 선택 앞에 놓입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“反正现在能跑，以后再重构”，只留下一条 TODO 注释就过去了。技术债越积越多，加新功能越来越慢，系统也越来越不稳定。到某一刻，就不得不面对“推倒重写”这种极端选择。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.041.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Start with tests for your core business logic. It doesn't have to be TDD at first; begin by adding tests after you write the code. Prioritize important logic by asking, 'Can I automatically verify that this function behaves correctly?'"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Start by writing tests for your core business logic. It doesn't have to be TDD at first; begin by adding tests after you write the code. Prioritise the important logic by asking: \"can I automatically check that this function behaves correctly?\""
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "핵심 비즈니스 로직부터 테스트를 작성하세요. 처음에는 TDD가 아니어도 됩니다. 코드 작성 후 테스트를 추가하는 것부터 시작하세요. '이 함수가 옳게 동작하는지 자동으로 확인할 수 있는가?'를 기준으로, 중요한 로직에 우선순위를 두세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "从核心业务逻辑开始写测试。一开始不必是 TDD，先从写完代码后补测试做起。以“能不能自动验证这个函数是否正确？”为标准，优先覆盖重要的逻辑。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.041.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tests aren't a chore; they're a source of confidence. With tests, you can refactor and add features without fear, and that creates a virtuous cycle of code quality."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tests are not a chore; they are the source of your confidence. With tests, you can refactor and add features without fear, and that creates a virtuous circle of code quality."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "테스트는 귀찮은 것이 아니라 자신감의 근원입니다. 테스트가 있으면 리팩토링과 기능 추가를 두려움 없이 할 수 있고, 이것이 코드 품질의 선순환을 만듭니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "测试不是麻烦事，而是自信的来源。有了测试，重构和加功能就不用担惊受怕，这会带来代码质量的良性循环。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.041.mistake" : {
