    "mistake.049.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You write tests even for obvious code like getters/setters and toString() to reach 100% coverage. Meanwhile, the tests for complex business logic are poor, and you spend your time maintaining meaningless tests."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You write tests even for self-evident code such as getters, setters and toString() to reach 100% coverage. Meanwhile the tests for the genuinely complex business logic are of poor quality, and you spend your time maintaining meaningless tests."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "getter/setter, toString() 같은 자명한 코드까지 테스트를 작성하여 100% 커버리지를 달성합니다. 하지만 정작 복잡한 비즈니스 로직의 테스트 품질은 낮고, 의미 없는 테스트 유지보수에 시간을 씁니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "连 getter/setter、toString() 这种一目了然的代码也写测试，达成 100% 覆盖率。可真正复杂的业务逻辑的测试质量很低，还要花时间维护没意义的测试。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.050.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fix a failing test right away, or delete it. 'I'll fix it later' mostly never comes. If a test fails, either the code is wrong or the test is wrong. Find the cause and fix it. If you set CI to block the build when a test fails, this takes care of itself."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fix a failing test straight away, or delete it. \"I'll fix it later\" mostly never comes. If a test fails, either the code is wrong or the test is wrong. Find the cause and fix it. If you set CI to block the build on test failure, this follows naturally."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "실패하는 테스트는 즉시 해결하거나 삭제하세요. '나중에 고치겠다'는 대부분 영원히 오지 않습니다. 테스트가 실패한다면 코드가 잘못되었거나 테스트가 잘못되었거나 둘 중 하나입니다. 원인을 파악하여 해결하세요. CI에서 테스트 실패 시 빌드가 차단되게 설정하면 자연스럽게 지켜집니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "失败的测试要么立即解决，要么删除。“以后再修”大多永远不会来。测试失败，要么是代码错了，要么是测试错了，二者必居其一，找出原因并解决。在 CI 里设置测试失败就阻断构建，自然就能坚持下来。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.050.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You build the habit of keeping your test suite healthy. Keeping the build green is team discipline, and a culture of not leaving broken windows unrepaired keeps code quality up."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You form the habit of keeping your test suite healthy. Keeping the build green is a matter of team discipline, and a culture of not leaving broken windows unrepaired is what maintains code quality."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "테스트 스위트의 건강 관리 습관을 들입니다. '그린 빌드(Green Build)'를 유지하는 것은 팀의 규율이며, 깨진 창문(Broken Window)을 방치하지 않는 문화가 코드 품질을 유지합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会养成维护测试套件健康的习惯。保持绿色构建（Green Build）是团队的纪律，不放任破窗（Broken Window）的文化能维持代码质量。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
