    "mistake.052.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you learn a new library, you start by searching blogs. You follow a post from 2019 written for v2, but the library is now at v5 and the API has changed completely. The outdated info costs you debugging time instead."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you learn a new library, you start by searching for blog posts. You follow a post from 2019 written for v2, but the current version is v5 and the API has changed completely. Outdated information leaves you wasting time on debugging."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "새로운 라이브러리를 배울 때 블로그 검색부터 합니다. 2019년에 작성된 v2 기준의 글을 따라 하는데 현재는 v5여서 API가 완전히 바뀌었습니다. 오래된 정보로 인해 오히려 디버깅에 시간을 낭비합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "学新库时，先去搜博客。照着 2019 年基于 v2 写的文章操作，可现在已经是 v5，API 完全变了。过时的信息反而让调试白白浪费时间。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.053.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Study CS fundamentals a little each week. Understand at least the core concepts of data structures (hash maps, trees, graphs), algorithms (sorting, searching, dynamic programming), networking (HTTP, TCP/IP), and operating systems (processes, threads, memory). Connecting them to problems you face at work helps the fundamentals sink in faster."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Study CS fundamentals a little each week. Understand at least the core ideas of data structures (hash maps, trees, graphs), algorithms (sorting, searching, dynamic programming), networking (HTTP, TCP/IP) and operating systems (processes, threads, memory). Linking them to problems you meet in real work helps the fundamentals sink in faster."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "매주 조금씩 CS 기초를 공부하세요. 자료구조(해시맵, 트리, 그래프), 알고리즘(정렬, 탐색, 동적 프로그래밍), 네트워크(HTTP, TCP/IP), 운영체제(프로세스, 스레드, 메모리)의 핵심 개념만이라도 이해하세요. 실무에서 직면하는 문제와 연결하면 기본기가 더 빨리 체화됩니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "每周学一点 CS 基础。哪怕只理解数据结构（哈希表、树、图）、算法（排序、搜索、动态规划）、网络（HTTP、TCP/IP）、操作系统（进程、线程、内存）的核心概念也好。把它和工作中遇到的问题联系起来，基本功会内化得更快。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.053.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Frameworks change, but the fundamentals stay. With solid CS basics, when you learn new technology you can quickly grasp the context: 'Ah, this is B-Tree based,' or 'This is the event loop pattern.'"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Frameworks change, but the fundamentals remain. With solid CS foundations, when you learn new technology you can quickly grasp the context: \"oh, this is built on a B-tree\", \"this is the event loop pattern\"."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "프레임워크는 바뀌지만 기본기는 남습니다. CS 기초가 탄탄하면 새로운 기술을 배울 때 '이건 B-Tree 기반이구나', '이건 이벤트 루프 패턴이구나'라며 빠르게 맥락을 파악할 수 있습니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "框架会变，基本功会留下来。CS 基础扎实，学新技术时就能很快抓住脉络：“这是基于 B-Tree 的”“这是事件循环模式”。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
