          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.057.retro.4" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How do you balance searching thoroughly before asking against asking quickly?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How do you balance searching thoroughly before asking against asking quickly?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "'질문하기 전에 충분히 찾아보기'와 '빨리 물어보기' 사이의 균형을 어떻게 잡고 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "在“提问前先充分查找”和“尽快开口问”之间，你怎么把握平衡？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.057.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When an unfamiliar technical term comes up in a meeting, you pretend you know it. You're assigned a task using a technology you've never touched and just say, 'I'll give it a try.' You struggle alone, the schedule slips, and by the time you ask for help it's already too late."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When a technical term comes up in a meeting that you don't know, you pretend you do. You're assigned a task using a technology you have no experience with, but you just say \"I'll give it a go\". You struggle alone, the schedule slips, and by the time you finally ask for help it's already too late."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "회의에서 잘 모르는 기술 용어가 나와도 아는 척합니다. 작업을 배정받았는데 경험이 없는 기술이지만 '해볼게요'라고만 합니다. 혼자 끙끙대다 일정이 밀리고, 결국 도움을 구할 때는 이미 늦은 상황입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "开会时听到不熟悉的技术术语，也假装懂。接到不熟悉的技术任务，只回一句“我试试”。一个人苦苦硬撑，进度拖延，等到求助时已经晚了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.058.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Feedback is about the code, not about you. Adopt the mindset that it's not 'my code' but 'the team's code.' When you receive feedback, first ask yourself, 'What can I learn from this comment?' When you disagree, talk it through constructively, but try to understand the other person's perspective first."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Feedback is about the code, not about you. Adopt the mindset that it's \"the team's code\", not \"my code\". When you receive feedback, first ask yourself, \"what can I learn from this comment?\" When you disagree, talk it through constructively, but try to understand the other person's point of view first."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "피드백은 코드에 대한 것이지 나에 대한 것이 아닙니다. '내 코드'가 아니라 '팀의 코드'라는 마인드셋을 가지세요. 피드백을 들을 때 '이 코멘트에서 배울 수 있는 것이 무엇인가?'를 먼저 생각하세요. 동의하지 않을 때는 건설적으로 대화하되, 상대의 관점을 먼저 이해하려고 노력하세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "反馈针对的是代码，不是你这个人。要有“这是团队的代码”而不是“这是我的代码”的心态。听到反馈时，先想“从这条评论里我能学到什么？”。不同意时，建设性地沟通，但要先努力理解对方的角度。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.058.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You build a growth mindset. How well you accept feedback determines how fast you grow. Developers who use code review as a chance to learn grow the fastest."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You develop a growth mindset. Your ability to accept feedback determines how fast you grow. Developers who use code review as a chance to learn grow the fastest."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "성장 마인드셋(Growth Mindset)을 기릅니다. 피드백을 수용하는 능력이 성장 속도를 결정합니다. 코드 리뷰를 학습의 기회로 활용하는 개발자가 가장 빠르게 성장합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会培养成长型思维（Growth Mindset）。接受反馈的能力决定成长的速度。把代码评审当作学习机会的开发者，成长得最快。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.058.mistake" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Taking feedback as a personal attack"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Taking feedback as a personal attack"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "피드백을 개인적인 공격으로 받아들인다"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "把反馈当成对个人的攻击"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.058.retro.1" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
