            "value" : "最近卡住的问题你一个人硬磕了多久？你遵守 15 分钟规则吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.062.retro.2" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you ask for help, do you share what you tried and your hypotheses?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you ask for help, do you share what you've tried and your hypotheses?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "도움을 요청할 때 자신의 시도와 가설을 함께 전달하고 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "求助时，你会连同自己的尝试和假设一起说明吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.062.retro.3" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has a problem ever been solved in five minutes after you asked for help? How much time had you spent alone first?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has asking for help ever solved a problem in five minutes? How long had you spent alone first?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "도움을 요청한 후 5분 만에 해결된 경험이 있나요? 혼자 얼마나 시간을 쓴 후였나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有没有求助后 5 分钟就解决的经历？在那之前你一个人花了多少时间？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.062.retro.4" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Are there feelings that make you hesitant to ask (like worrying you'll look incompetent)? Are they reasonable?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Is there a feeling that makes you reluctant to ask for help, such as fear of looking incompetent? Is that feeling reasonable?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "도움 요청을 꺼리게 만드는 감정(무능하게 보일까 봐 등)이 있나요? 그 감정이 합리적인가요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有没有什么情绪让你不愿求助（比如怕显得无能）？这种情绪合理吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.062.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Afraid that people will think 'They can't even solve this,' you wrestle with the same problem for two or three days. The schedule slips, and when you finally ask a senior, it's solved in five minutes. The time you spent alone ends up delaying the whole team's schedule."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Afraid that people will think you're incompetent if you can't solve it, you stay stuck on the same problem for two or three days. The schedule slips, and when you finally ask a senior, it's solved in five minutes. The time you spent agonising alone ends up delaying the whole team's schedule."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "'이것도 못 풀면 무능하다고 생각하겠지'라는 두려움에 2~3일째 같은 문제에 매달립니다. 결국 일정이 밀리고, 시니어에게 물어보니 5분 만에 해결됩니다. 혼자 고민한 시간이 팀 전체의 일정을 지연시킨 결과가 됩니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "因为害怕“连这个都解决不了，会被觉得无能”，在同一个问题上硬磕两三天。结果进度延误，去问了资深同事，5 分钟就解决了。一个人纠结的时间，最终拖慢了整个团队的进度。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.063.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Write Architecture Decision Records (ADRs). The format is simple: 1) context (what's the situation?), 2) decision (what did you choose?), 3) rationale (why?), 4) alternatives (what were the other options?), 5) consequences (what impact do you expect?). Keep them in a /docs/adr folder in the project repository."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Write Architecture Decision Records (ADRs). The format is simple: 1) context (what was the situation?), 2) decision (what was chosen?), 3) rationale (why?), 4) alternatives (what were the other options?), 5) consequences (what impact is expected?). Create a /docs/adr folder in the project repository to keep them in."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Architecture Decision Records(ADR)를 작성하세요. 형식은 간단합니다: 1) 컨텍스트(어떤 상황?), 2) 결정(무엇을 선택?), 3) 이유(왜?), 4) 대안(다른 옵션은?), 5) 결과(예상 영향은?). 프로젝트 저장소에 /docs/adr 폴더를 만들어 관리하세요."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "写架构决策记录（ADR，Architecture Decision Records）。格式很简单：1) 背景（什么情况？）；2) 决策（选了什么？）；3) 理由（为什么？）；4) 备选方案（还有哪些选项？）；5) 结果（预期有什么影响？）。在项目仓库里建一个 /docs/adr 目录来管理。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.063.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You learn how to build organizational memory. ADRs speed up onboarding for new teammates, prevent the same discussion from repeating, and raise the quality of decisions."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You learn to build organisational memory. ADRs speed up the onboarding of new teammates, prevent the same discussions repeating and improve the quality of decisions."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "조직적 기억(Organizational Memory)을 만드는 능력을 배웁니다. ADR은 새로운 팀원의 온보딩을 가속화하고, 같은 논의의 반복을 방지하며, 의사결정의 질을 높입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会学到建立组织记忆（Organizational Memory）的能力。ADR 能加快新成员的入职，避免重复讨论，提高决策质量。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.063.mistake" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
