          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你有没有用比喻或可视化的方式解释过？对方反应如何？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.065.retro.4" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has a dev team request ever been rejected or deprioritized because it wasn't explained well enough?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has a lack of explanation ever led to the development team's request being rejected or deprioritised?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "설명이 부족해서 개발팀의 요청이 기각되거나 우선순위에서 밀린 경험이 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有没有因为解释不到位，导致开发团队的请求被驳回或被排到后面？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.065.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You tell a product manager, 'API latency is high, so we need to introduce an async queue to decouple it.' The PM has no idea what that means, and the dev team's request gets rejected or pushed down the priority list."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You tell the product manager, \"API latency is high, so we need to introduce an asynchronous queue to decouple it.\" The product manager has no idea what you mean, and the development team's request is turned down or pushed down the priority list."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "'API의 레이턴시가 높아서 비동기 큐를 도입해 데커플링해야 합니다'라고 기획자에게 말합니다. 기획자는 무슨 말인지 모르고, 개발팀의 요청이 거절되거나 우선순위에서 밀립니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "对产品经理说“API 延迟太高，需要引入异步队列来解耦”。产品经理听不懂，开发团队的请求被驳回，或者被排到后面。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apply a buffer of 1.5 to 3 times to your estimates. Break the work into the smallest units you can and estimate each one. Use the rule of thumb optimistic estimate × 2 = realistic estimate. State the uncertain parts explicitly: 'The basic feature is three days; the API integration has an external dependency and could add one to three days.'"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Add a buffer of 1.5 to 3 times to your estimates. Break the work into the smallest pieces you can and estimate each one. Use \"optimistic estimate × 2 = realistic estimate\" as a rule of thumb. State the uncertain parts explicitly: \"The basic feature takes three days; the API integration has an external dependency and could add one to three days.\""
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "추정치에 1.5~3배의 버퍼를 적용하세요. 작업을 최대한 작은 단위로 쪼개서 각각을 추정하세요. '낙관적 추정 × 2 = 현실적 추정'을 경험칙으로 사용하세요. 불확실한 부분은 명시적으로 밝히세요: '기본 기능은 3일, API 연동은 외부 의존성이 있어 1~3일 추가될 수 있습니다.'"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "给估算值加 1.5~3 倍的缓冲。把任务尽量拆小，分别估算。用“乐观估算 × 2 = 现实估算”作为经验法则。对不确定的部分要明确说明：“基础功能 3 天，接口对接有外部依赖，可能再多 1~3 天。”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "An estimate is a prediction, not a promise. The ability to state uncertainty explicitly is worth more than an accurate estimate. This skill is central to project management and builds trust."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "An estimate is a forecast, not a promise. The ability to state your uncertainty is worth more than an accurate estimate. This skill is the core of project management and builds trust."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "추정은 약속이 아니라 예측입니다. 정확한 추정보다 '불확실성을 명시하는' 능력이 더 가치 있습니다. 이 능력은 프로젝트 관리의 핵심이며, 신뢰를 구축합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "估算不是承诺，而是预测。比起精准的估算，“明确指出不确定性”的能力更有价值。这是项目管理的核心，也能建立信任。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.mistake" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Estimating development schedules far too optimistically"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Being far too optimistic when estimating development schedules"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "개발 일정 추정을 지나치게 낙관적으로 한다"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "估算开发工期过于乐观"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.retro.1" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How far off was your last estimate from what actually happened? (as a percentage)"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How far off was your last schedule estimate from reality? (As a percentage)"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "마지막으로 한 일정 추정이 실제와 얼마나 차이가 났나요? (비율로)"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你上一次的工期估算和实际差了多少？（用比例表示）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.retro.2" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Do your estimates include code review, writing tests, and unexpected issues?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Do you include code review, writing tests and unexpected issues in your estimates?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "추정 시 코드 리뷰, 테스트 작성, 예상 못한 이슈를 포함시키고 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "估算时，你把代码评审、写测试和意外问题算进去了吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.retro.3" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Do you state the uncertain parts explicitly? (for example, 'at least 3 days, at most 7')"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Do you state the uncertain parts explicitly, such as \"at least three days, at most seven\"?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "불확실한 부분을 명시적으로 밝히고 있나요? ('최소 3일, 최대 7일'처럼)"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你会明确说出不确定的部分吗？（比如“最少 3 天，最多 7 天”）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.retro.4" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If your estimates are repeatedly wrong, have you analyzed the pattern?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If your estimates are wrong again and again, have you ever analysed the pattern?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "추정이 반복적으로 틀린다면 그 패턴을 분석해본 적이 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "如果估算总是不准，你分析过其中的规律吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.066.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You say, 'It'll take three days,' but it actually takes a week. Unexpected technical hurdles, the complexity of existing code, code review and rework, bug fixes, and deployment prep were all missing from the estimate. If you keep overrunning, you lose the team's trust."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You say \"three days should do it\", but it actually takes a week. Unexpected technical hurdles, the complexity of the existing code, code review and rework, bug fixing and release preparation were all missing from the estimate. If you overrun again and again, you lose the team's trust."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "'3일이면 됩니다'라고 말하지만 실제로는 일주일이 걸립니다. 예상하지 못한 기술적 장벽, 기존 코드의 복잡도, 코드 리뷰와 수정, 버그 수정, 배포 준비 등이 추정에 빠져 있었습니다. 반복적으로 일정을 초과하면 팀의 신뢰를 잃습니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "嘴上说“3 天就行”，实际要一周。没预料到的技术障碍、现有代码的复杂度、代码评审与修改、修 Bug、部署准备等，都没算进估算里。反复超期，会失去团队的信任。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.067.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Invest just 10 minutes before implementing to pin down the requirements. Ask: 'Is search triggered in real time or by a button click?' 'Which fields are searched?' 'What do we show when there are no results?' 'Do we need pagination?' Reviewing a wireframe or mockup together dramatically cuts misunderstandings."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spend just ten minutes before implementing to pin the requirements down. Check things like: \"is the search triggered live or by a button?\", \"which fields are searched?\", \"what do we show when there are no results?\", \"do we need pagination?\" Going through wireframes or mock-ups together dramatically reduces misunderstandings."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "구현 전에 10분만 투자하여 요구사항을 구체화하세요: '검색 트리거가 실시간인가 버튼 클릭인가?', '검색 대상 필드가 무엇인가?', '결과가 없을 때 어떻게 표시하나?', '페이지네이션이 필요한가?' 등을 확인하세요. 와이어프레임이나 목업을 함께 확인하면 오해를 극적으로 줄일 수 있습니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "实现之前花 10 分钟把需求具体化：“搜索是实时触发还是点按钮？”“搜索哪些字段？”“没有结果时怎么显示？”“需要分页吗？”等等。一起看线框图或原型，能大幅减少误解。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.067.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Requirements analysis is the first and most important step in development. Building the right thing roughly is always better than building the wrong thing well."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Requirements analysis is the first and most important step of development. Building the right thing roughly is always better than building the wrong thing well."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "요구사항 분석(Requirements Analysis) 능력은 개발의 첫 단계이자 가장 중요한 단계입니다. 맞는 것을 대충 만드는 게 틀린 것을 잘 만드는 것보다 항상 낫습니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "需求分析（Requirements Analysis）能力是开发的第一步，也是最重要的一步。把对的事情粗略做出来，总比把错的事情做得漂亮要好。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.067.mistake" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Jumping into implementation without confirming the requirements"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Starting to implement without confirming the requirements"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "요구사항을 확인하지 않고 바로 구현에 들어간다"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "不确认需求就直接动手实现"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.067.retro.1" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
