        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "只坚持自己的意见，不听其他观点"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.069.retro.1" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In technical discussions, do you try to find the strengths in the other person's idea first?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In technical discussions, do you try to find the strengths in the other person's view first?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "기술 토론에서 상대 의견의 장점을 먼저 찾으려 노력하고 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "技术讨论中，你会先尽量找出对方意见的优点吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.069.retro.2" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Have you recently admitted that your opinion was wrong? How did that feel?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Have you admitted recently that you were wrong? How did that feel?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "내 의견이 틀렸다는 것을 인정한 적이 최근에 있나요? 그때 어떤 감정이었나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你最近承认过自己的意见是错的吗？当时是什么心情？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.069.retro.3" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Do you enter conversations assuming you could be wrong, or do you start from 'I'm right'?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Do you talk on the assumption that you might be wrong, or do you start from \"I'm right\"?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "'내가 틀릴 수 있다'는 전제로 대화하고 있나요? 아니면 '내가 맞다'부터 시작하나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你是带着“我可能是错的”的前提交流，还是从“我是对的”开始？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.069.retro.4" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has combining multiple perspectives ever led to a better solution?"
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Has combining several viewpoints ever produced a better solution?"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "여러 관점을 통합하여 더 나은 해결책이 나온 경험이 있나요?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有没有整合多种观点而得到更好方案的经历？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.069.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In technical discussions you keep repeating 'My way is right' and don't listen to other opinions. The other person gets defensive too, and it becomes an emotional argument instead of a constructive discussion. In the end you miss a better solution."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In technical discussions, you keep repeating \"my way is right\" and don't listen to other opinions. The other person becomes defensive too, and the conversation turns into an emotional argument instead of a constructive debate. In the end you miss out on a better solution."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "기술 토론에서 '제 방법이 맞습니다'를 반복하며 다른 의견을 듣지 않습니다. 상대방도 방어적으로 변하고, 건설적인 토론이 아닌 감정적 논쟁이 됩니다. 결국 더 좋은 해결책을 놓칩니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "技术讨论中一再强调“我的方法是对的”，听不进别的意见。对方也变得有防备，讨论不再有建设性，而是变成情绪化的争吵。最终错过了更好的方案。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.070.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Make documentation part of your development process. Put 'update related docs' in your PR definition of done. At the very least, maintain a README (install/run instructions), API docs (endpoints, requests/responses), and an architecture overview. Docs that are better than nothing matter more than perfect docs."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Make documentation part of your development process. Put \"update related documentation\" in your definition of done for PRs. At the very least, maintain a README (how to install and run), API docs (endpoints, requests and responses) and an architecture overview. Documentation that is better than nothing matters more than perfect documentation."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "문서화를 개발 프로세스의 일부로 포함시키세요. PR 완료 조건에 '관련 문서 업데이트'를 넣으세요. 최소한 README(설치/실행 방법), API 문서(엔드포인트, 요청/응답), 아키텍처 개요 문서를 유지하세요. 완벽한 문서보다 '없는 것보다 나은' 문서가 중요합니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "把写文档纳入开发流程。在 PR 完成条件里加上“更新相关文档”。至少保持 README（安装/运行方法）、API 文档（接口、请求/响应）和架构概览文档。比起完美的文档，更重要的是“比没有强”的文档。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.070.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Documentation determines your team's scalability. A well-documented project cuts onboarding from weeks to days and reduces bus factor risk, where knowledge is concentrated in one person."
          }
        },
        "en-GB" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Documentation determines a team's scalability. A well-documented project cuts onboarding time from weeks to days and reduces the bus factor risk of knowledge being concentrated in particular individuals."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "문서화는 팀의 확장성(Scalability)을 결정합니다. 잘 문서화된 프로젝트는 온보딩 시간을 수 주에서 수 일로 줄이고, 지식이 특정 개인에게 집중되는 버스 팩터(Bus Factor) 리스크를 줄입니다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "文档决定团队的可扩展性（Scalability）。文档完善的项目，能把新人上手时间从几周缩短到几天，也能降低知识集中在个别人身上的巴士系数（Bus Factor）风险。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.070.mistake" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
